# The image every CI job that compiles anything runs in. One line, read by
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and by `e2e/ci-image-check.mjs`.
#
# THREE PARTS, ALL LOAD-BEARING. The digest is what is pulled — a tag can be moved by anyone who can
# push to the registry, a digest cannot, and it is what answers "which environment built
# this binary". The tag is the hash of what the image is made of: `Containerfile`,
# `rust-toolchain.toml`, `.node-version`, and the `packageManager` line of package.json.
#
# The date makes the tag immutable: a reused tag untags the previous manifest, GHCR
# collects it, and every pin stops resolving at once — which is what happened on
# 2026-11-19. `ci-image-check` recomputes that hash and fails if it is not the tag below. So editing
# any of those four files without republishing the image fails CI with the reason, instead
# of silently validating the change in the environment it was meant to replace.
#
# To move it: run the `Toolchain image` workflow (it runs itself weekly, and on a push
# that touches those files), then paste the line it prints here.
